  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8ba18922ef01d4d4c8990ab10d716134, type: 3}
  m_Name: Slide17
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questionText: Intersections of this diagonal line with lines parallel to AB at
    A4, A3, A2 and A1 are respectively at 0.2cm, 0.4 cm, 0.6 cm and 0.8 cm.
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: 'The diagonal line divides 1 cm into five equal divisions. According
    to the law of proportional similarity, for 5 equal divisions, the given line
    will be divided into sections of lengths 0.2 cm. As a result, 0.2 cm is the least
    count of the scale in this case.


    Hence the intercepts must be at 0.2 cm,
    0.4 cm, 0.6 cm and 0.8 cm marks, respectively.'
  options:
  - True
  - False
  correctOptionIndex: 0
  correctDropId: 
  correctValue: 0
  tolerance: 0.1
